  "result": "I fixed it: `Cart.remove` now removes the Widget line, and all the tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** In `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` filtered lines by `l.item.name != sku`. That compared the SKU you passed in (`'sku-1'`) against the item's display name (`'Widget'`). They never match, so nothing was removed. `Cart.add` matches on `item.sku`, so `remove` was inconsistent with it.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the comparison to `l.item.sku != sku`.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, so only the Gadget is left. Before the fix it printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest`: 6 tests, all OK.\n\nNone of the existing tests cover `Cart.remove`, which is why this bug got through. I can add a small regression test in a new `tests/test_models.py` if you'd like.",
